iOS 27, the Metal plug-in's frontend: a no-copy buffer over memory this process may never write is made over a copy of its bytes.
backboardd's no-copy buffers over CoreAnimation's images that other processes share read-only (VM tag 51, prot 1/1, share
mode 5) are memory the kernel's IMPORT_HOST cannot wire either way, so PanVK's import failed, metal2vulkan answered
Unsupported(HostMemory, NotRepresentable) and the frontend returned nil: the app switcher's non-live cards drew black.
Nothing in backboardd can write those pages and CoreAnimation only samples them, so the buffer now holds a copy taken when it
is made; the caller's deallocator still runs when the buffer goes. A range with any page whose maximum protection allows a
write is refused as before (a copy would no longer alias bytes its caller writes). SWEET_MTL2_NOCOPY_RO=0 gives the old answer.
The first 8 copies (then every power of two) log "native-metal: no-copy read-only memory ... copied (N so far)".
Applied after frontend-nocopy-diag.diff (its refusal line is then only for memory that is still refused).
